{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1092", "sample_idx": 6, "model_name": "google/gemma-3n-e4b-it", "content": "## Lost (and Found) in Japan\n\nJapan. The word itself conjures images of ancient temples, bustling cityscapes, and serene gardens. My recent trip lived up to every expectation – and then some!\n\nI started in Tokyo, a sensory overload in the best way possible. Neon lights, delicious ramen, and the organized chaos of Shibuya crossing – it was exhilarating. I spent days exploring vibrant neighborhoods like Shinjuku and Harajuku, soaking in the unique street style and quirky shops.\n\nFrom Tokyo, I took the Shinkansen (bullet train!) to Kyoto. The contrast was striking. Here, I wandered through tranquil bamboo forests, visited stunning golden pavilions, and experienced a traditional tea ceremony. Gion, Kyoto's geisha district, felt like stepping back in time.\n\nFood was a constant highlight. From delicate sushi to savory okonomiyaki, every meal was an adventure. I even braved (and enjoyed!) takoyaki – octopus balls!\n\nBeyond the iconic sights, it was the small moments that truly stood out: the impeccable politeness of the people, the meticulous attention to detail in everything, and the feeling of being both completely immersed in a different culture and surprisingly welcomed.\n\nJapan is a country of contrasts – ancient traditions alongside cutting-edge technology. It’s a place that challenges and delights, leaving you wanting more. I can't wait to go back!\n", "logprobs": [{"token": "##", "logprob": -1.6689286894688848e-06}, {"token": "▁Lost", "logprob": -0.0011177966371178627}, {"token": "▁(", "logprob": -0.18502815067768097}, {"token": "and", "logprob": -8.344646857949556e-07}, {"token": "▁Found", "logprob": -0.0015026956098154187}, {"token": ")", "logprob": -0.1426810771226883}, {"token": "▁in", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "▁Japan", "logprob": -0.11408442258834839}, {"token": "\n\n", "logprob": -0.25964632630348206}, {"token": "Japan", "logprob": -0.60